The Ta/Fe–Mn-Si MMC (0.5 wt.% Ta) specimens were fabricated using a Concept Laser 200R LPBF 3D printer with a 200 W continuous wave laser and an 80 μm laser spot size in a high-purity argon environment with less than 0.3% oxygen. A bidirectional scan strategy with a 90-degree layer rotation was employed, maintaining a layer thickness of 0.03 mm and hatch spacing of 0.1 mm. A 100 mm/s laser scanning speed and 200 W laser power were used for producing both 5 × 5 × 5 mm 3  cubes for microstructural investigations and dog-bone-shaped tensile bars (see Fig.  S1  of the Supplementary Information) for mechanical testing. The volumetric laser energy density (VED) was calculated to be 166.67 J/mm 3  according to: 1 V E D = P h × t × v , \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
